{\bf (Automorphism Problem.)}
Is it true that
$$\lim _{n\to \infty } \max _{|P|=n}
{ |{\rm Aut} (P)|\over |{\rm End} (P)| } =0?$$

\label{blockdef}

Let $G$ be a permutation group on the set $X$.
A subset $B\subseteq X$ is called a {\bf ($G$-)block}
iff, for all $\sigma \in G$, we have
     
$\sigma [B]=B$ or $\sigma [B]\cap B=\emptyset $.
A block is called {\bf nontrivial} iff it is not
a singleton and not equal to
$X$.
A transitive permutation group $G$ is called {\bf primitive}
iff it has no nontrivial $G$-blocks.

\label{restrictonK}

Let $(U,{\cal D} , G^*
)$ be a
standard configuration,
let $G'$ be a subgroup of $G^* $,
and let
${\cal K}
$ be a set of blocks for $G^* $.
We define
$$G' _{\searrow  {\cal K} }
:=\left\{
\Phi \in G' :
(\forall K\in {\cal K} )
\Phi \! \Rsh  ^{\Lambda  ^* (D_K )\cdot K }
=
{\rm id} \! \Rsh  ^{\Lambda  ^* (D_K )\cdot K }
\right\} .
$$
In cases in which ${\cal K}$ can be easily enumerated
as ${\cal K} =\{ B_1 , \ldots , B_n \} $, we will
write
$G' _{\searrow  B_1 , \ldots , B_n } $
instead of
$G' _{\searrow  \{ B_1 , \ldots , B_n \} } $.

\label{normalgrouplem}

Let $(U,{\cal D} , G^*
)$ be a
standard configuration,
let $G'$ be a subgroup of $G^* $,
and let
${\cal K}
$ be a set of blocks for $G^* $.
Then $G' _{\searrow  {\cal K} } $
is a normal subgroup of $G' $.
Moreover,
for every
$B\not\in
{\cal K} $, the factor
group
$G' _{\searrow  {\cal K} } /
G' _{\searrow  {\cal K} \cup \{ B\} } $
is isomorphic to
$\left\{
\Phi
\! \Rsh  ^{\Lambda  ^* (D_B )\cdot B }
:
\Phi \in
G' _{\searrow  {\cal K} }
\right\}
$.

\label{fixedbyprevious}

Let $(U,{\cal D} , G^* ; {\cal B})$ be a nested
standard configuration,
let
${\cal K} \subseteq {\cal B}$
and let $B\in {\cal B}\setminus {\cal K}$.
We define
\begin{eqnarray*}
\Lambda  ^* \left( {\cal K}\not\searrow  B \right)
& := &
\left\{
\Phi
\! \Rsh  ^{\Lambda  ^* (D_B )\cdot B }
:
\Phi \in
G' _{\searrow  {\cal K} }
\right\}
.
\end{eqnarray*}

\label{1.54bound}

Let $1\leq c_0 <c_1 <\cdots <c_m =x$ be natural numbers such that,
for all $j\in \{ 0,\ldots , m-1\} $, the quotient
${c_{j+1} \over c_j } $
is an integer greater than or equal to $2$.
Then
$
\prod _{j=0} ^{m-1}
2^{ d_{
c_{j+1}
/ c_j }
{
x
\over
c_j }
}
\leq
2^{1.54 {x\over c_0 } } .$

\label{reindexed}

Let
$\left( U,{\cal D} , G^* ; \overrightarrow{{\cal B}} \right)$
be an enumerated nested
standard configuration,
and let $\gamma _{\cal B} ^* $ be a control function.
Then
$\displaystyle{
\left| G^* \right|
\leq
\prod _{D\in {\cal D}}
\Omega _{{\cal B} } \left( D\right)
\leq
2^{0.99|U|}
\prod _{D\in {\cal D}}
\Upsilon _{{\cal B} } \left( D\right)
.
}$

\label{upperboundonlyoutsizedleft}

Let
$\left( U,{\cal D} , G^* ; {\cal B} \right)$
be a nested\textsuperscript{\ref{primnestcoll}}
standard configuration\textsuperscript{\ref{standardconfdef}}
and let ${\cal U}$ be the set of
undersized\textsuperscript{\ref{outsizedef}}
components
of
$({\cal F},\blacksquare )$\textsuperscript{\ref{mutualmaxlockdef}}
of vertex width\textsuperscript{\ref{lowerandupperlevels}} $w\geq 5$.
Then
there is a
reverse depth enumeration\textsuperscript{\ref{RDEdef}}
$\overrightarrow{\cal B} $
of ${\cal B}$
with a control function\textsuperscript{\ref{controlfunction}}
$\gamma _{\cal B} ^* $
such that
$\displaystyle{
\left| G^* \right|
\leq
2^{0.99 |U|}
\prod _{D\in {\cal D} }
\Upsilon _{{\cal B} } (D)
} $, and
such that
${\cal B} _u ^\gamma
\subseteq L({\cal U}) $.

\label{width9}

The Automorphism Conjecture is true for
the class ${\cal W} _9 $ of ordered sets of width at most $9$.
